xt":"Brivio retires; his radiator was burst on Hartmann's tail on the first lap.","q":false,"c":11},{"lap":23,"text":"On lap 23 Kautz stopped the Mercedes-Benz to have spark plugs replaced and refueled in two minutes.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":2},{"lap":23,"text":"On the same lap Stuck stopped for 1m30s to have his brakes adjusted and refueled as well, falling back from 5th to 8th place","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":3},{"lap":28,"text":"Biondetti (Maserati) retired on lap 28 with engine problems.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":10},{"lap":30,"text":"The battle between Caracciola and Brauchitsch continued ahead of Zehender in third place one lap behind and Farina who was two laps back.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi"},{"lap":35,"text":"On lap 35 Pintacuda stopped and was exchanged at the wheel by Trossi.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":8},{"lap":38,"text":"Three laps later, Stuck stopped for new plugs, Rosemeyer relieved him at the wheel, when in seventh place.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":3},{"lap":40,"text":"Caracciola remained in the lead ahead of Brauchitsch with Zehender third, followed by Farina and Kautz.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":47,"text":"On lap 47 Caracciola came rolling into the pit with an enormous noise from the engine. A mechanic found a screw that had dropped out of the induction pipe, which was duly replaced.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":50,"text":"Brauchitsch leads by two minutes; Caracciola is now a lap behind.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":50,"text":"Trossi hands the car over to Pintacuda.","c":8},{"lap":51,"text":"Four Mercedes were in the top positions after Kautz passed Farina on lap 51.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":2},{"lap":55,"text":"On lap 55 Caracciola unlapped himself as Brauchitsch waved him by on the Promenade","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":64,"text":"For the next ten laps Caracciola steadily gained on Brauchitsch and on lap 64 he did a lap in 1m47.9s.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":68,"text":"Stuck hands the car over to Rosemeyer.","c":3},{"lap":69,"text":"Brauchitsch stops for fuel and tyres; a locked front brake costs him 1m30s and he rejoins just in front of Caracciola.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":69,"text":"Hartmann (Maserati) retired on the 69th lap","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":9},{"lap":74,"text":"Caracciola breaks the lap record again with 1m46.5s.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":80,"text":"Brauchitsch finally lets Caracciola through.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":80,"text":"Rosemeyer, back in Stuck's car, laps in 1m48.8s and closes on Farina.","q":false,"c":3},{"lap":82,"text":"Caracciola stopped on lap 82 for fuel, tires and plugs and left after 1m25s. Brauchitsch took the lead again with Caracciola now nearly a lap behind.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":87,"text":"Rosemeyer shot past Farina's Alfa Romeo on the climb to the Casino, going now after Zehender.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":3},{"lap":90,"text":"Brauchitsch now drove steadily over half a lap ahead of Caracciola, followed by Kautz and Zehender who both were three laps behind.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":96,"text":"Rosemeyer chased after the fourth Mercedes of Zehender and passed him on lap 96 to gain fourth place.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":3},{"lap":100,"text":"Brauchitsch began the last lap to the ovations of the crowd and, successively, the opponents came to stop in front of the stands, while the German anthem was played, in homage to the winner.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":100,"text":"Von Brauchitsch wins from Caracciola, with Kautz a distant third; Stuck/Rosemeyer fourth, Zehender fifth, Farina sixth.","q":false,"c":0}]}